  "notes": [
    "scene.xml and right_sharpa_wave.xml are git-native (copied from UniLab src/unilab/assets/robots/sharpa_wave/, right_sharpa_wave.xml is byte-identical to UniLab git HEAD; scene.xml differs by the post-migration simple=\"false\" fix noted below); the HF unilab-robots dataset does not host sharpa_wave XML files.",
    "caches/sharpa_grasp_linspace is a filename prefix, not a directory: the runtime resolves '<grasp_cache_path>_<scale:g>.npy' (see UniLab sharpa_inhand resolve_grasp_cache_file), so cache files stay flat under caches/.",
    "right_sharpa_wave.usda was requested but does not exist in any unilabsim HF dataset (unilab-robots, unilab-caches, unilab-motions, unilab-scenes, unilab-checkpoints all checked).",
    "scene.xml: object body sets simple=\"false\" (post-migration fix); with the default simple/sameframe compilation, reset-time com/mass domain randomization trips mj_setConst \"sameframe no longer holds\" and crashes the mujoco_uni batch runtime.",
    "Manager-Based fixed variants add scene_scale_{0.8..1.5}.xml and right_sharpa_wave_manager.xml. The manager XML uniquely names every body geom and uses repo-relative mesh paths for mjbatch fixed-variant compilation; all variant XMLs retain object body simple=\"false\"."
  ],
